  "user_request_original": "Optimize a 29-layer planar multilayer thin film stack on fused silica substrate with air incidence. Layer sequence: layers 1-14 alternate HfO2 and MgF2 (Rodriguez-de_Marcos) starting with HfO2 (odd layers HfO2, even layers MgF2 (Rodriguez-de_Marcos)), layer 15 is HfO2 cavity defect, layers 16-29 alternate MgF2 (Rodriguez-de_Marcos) and HfO2 ending with HfO2 (odd layers MgF2 (Rodriguez-de_Marcos), even layers HfO2 in this section). Substrate material is SiO2 (Gao). Optimize individual layer thicknesses with position-dependent bounds relative to quarter-wave optical thickness baseline at 267.5 nm center wavelength: layers 0-3 and 25-28 (0-indexed) bounded to ±1.0 nm, layers 10-18 bounded to ±3.0 nm, all other layers bounded to ±2.5 nm. Apply curvature regularization with weight 0.15 to the second-difference of the thickness vector. Spectral objectives: maximize transmittance in 255-280 nm, minimize transmittance in 300-700 nm, minimize transmittance in 700-1100 nm. Total layer count fixed at 29. No metal layers. Use gradient-based thickness optimization.",
